sxml transform - Transform a document with an XSLT 4.0 stylesheet

Usage: sxml transform [--initial-mode=NAME] [--initial-template=NAME] [--method=METHOD] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... STYLESHEET [INPUT]

Compiles the XSLT 4.0 stylesheet STYLESHEET and runs it.

With INPUT, the document becomes the global context item. Templates
are applied to it in the default mode, or in the mode that
--initial-mode names; or the template that --initial-template names is
called with INPUT as the context item. Without INPUT, the template
that --initial-template names, else xsl:initial-template, is called
without a context item.

The principal result goes to standard output, serialized as the
stylesheet's xsl:output says; --method replaces the method. Result
documents with an href are not written. xsl:message output goes to
standard error. --param=NAME=VALUE binds the stylesheet parameter
$NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE). Included and imported modules and
documents are read from local files.

An error is reported on standard error as
  STYLESHEET:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 for an error in the stylesheet or a
document that is not well-formed, 3 when a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help                   Show this help and exit
      --initial-mode=NAME      Mode whose template rules process INPUT, instead of the default mode
      --initial-template=NAME  Named template to call, instead of applying templates to INPUT
      --method=METHOD          Serialization method of the result, replacing the stylesheet's (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json)
      --param=NAME=VALUE       Bind stylesheet parameter $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)

Arguments:
  STYLESHEET  File holding the principal stylesheet module
  INPUT       XML document to transform, the global context item; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml transform list.xsl books.xml
  sxml transform --param='heading=Reading list' list.xsl books.xml
  sxml transform hello.xsl
  sxml transform --method=xml list.xsl - < books.xml
